+# Summary: `--format markdown` for stockreport
+
+## Changed
+- `stockreport/report.py`: `render(items, "markdown")` now renders a GitHub-flavoured table with the `tabulate` pipe style (already used by the project's vendored `tabulate`). Same columns and order as the text report, prices with two decimals, numeric columns right-aligned. Output ends with a blank line and `**Total stock value:** <value>`. Pipes (`|`) in SKU and name are escaped as `\|` so they can't split a table row. The text output is unchanged.
+- `stockreport/__main__.py`: `--format` now accepts `markdown` as well as `text`.
+- `tests/test_markdown_escape.py` (new): checks pipe escaping in markdown, that text output is not escaped, and that an unknown format raises `ValueError`.
+- `README.md`: documents the new option.
+
+No existing test was edited or deleted. `vendor/` and dependencies are untouched.
+
+## Verified
+- `python -m unittest` (from the project root): 6 tests, all pass. This includes the pre-existing `test_markdown_output` and `test_cli_markdown`, which failed before the change (`unknown format 'markdown'` and `invalid choice`).
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv --format markdown`: output matches the expected table in `tests/test_report.py` exactly.
+- `python -m stockreport inventory.csv`: text output is unchanged.
+
+## Not verified / notes
+- I did not render the markdown on GitHub itself, so the table rendering is checked only against the expected text, not visually.
+- I ran the CLI without `python -I`, because `-I` removes the working directory from `sys.path` and the package then can't be imported by `-m`. The tests were run with plain `python -m unittest`.
+- The pipe escaping is my addition beyond the spec. Revert it if you don't want it.
+- `vendor/tabulate` README says the fork is owned by the platform team. I did not change it. Note its `pipe` style does not escape cell content itself, which is why escaping lives in `report.py`.
+- The `sys.exit(main())` at module level in `__main__.py` was already there; I did not change it.
